From b1fe4dd4d8cefc9ee01b2aa0248189b361576943 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:22:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] 1.3.96: the three voices alike, a ROLE each (Chord,
 Loops, Bass); envelopes AMB, Patch or ADSR

- every voice set the same way: its page Level, Role, Octave, Density; its Play page Envelope, Gate, Pace, Glide; a
  new ADSR page. Any voice any role (all three chords, if wanted), each with four notes (12 at most, as before 11);
  a voice changing role fades out and in (20 ms)
- PACE: a chord's breath (4..16 s), the loops' step (1/16..1/2), the bass struck each chord or each bar..1/8
- ENVELOPE: AMB-1's own, the patch's (now the default: each note struck and let go at GATE) or the ADSR (the
  carriers' envelope from four knobs, the modulators the patch's)
- AMB-1's eighteen patches for every voice (six pads, six bells, six basses), then the banks
- project format 9: the layers' settings of before (Swell, Density, Bell oct, Bass oct, Glide, Fifth) into each
  voice's (en_upgrade), the sources renumbered; formats 7 and 8 keep their patches; the pieces' recipes alike
- OCT- / OCT+ the voice shown's octave; MIDI CC 102..112 how each voice plays

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
